{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792397966,"nonce":"7qq1zMlpLN6PZB7F4IaLSir+OLM=","title":"LSP URI and path handling only decodes %20","message":"`uri_to_path` (`lsp/src/context.rs:297`) and `uri_to_file_path` (`lsp/src/server.rs:487`) strip `file://` and replace only `%20`. Any other percent-encoding (`%23`, unicode, `%3A` on Windows drive letters) gives a wrong path. Windows `file:///C:/...` produces `/C:/...`. Going back, `format!(\"file://{}\", path)` does not encode the path. Use `Uri`/`url` conversion both ways.","files":null}]}